Subject: Port: start without the boot loading message
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A presentation change of the port, always on and without a switch (owner
decision, 2026-10-14). It lives in the tweak series so the faithful series
stays retail.

Right after glStartup, original main calls DisplayLoadingMessageFast
(LidOpenMessage.cpp). It turns the video output black, pokes the localized
128x32 one-bit "Loading" bitmap into both external frame buffers and shows it
until the boot scene's first frame. On a desktop display those are a few large
white pixels on black, right after the port's graphics preparation screen.
Main now skips that call. The output stays black, and the boot scene's first
swap turns it on, as glxSwap already does after every black interval. The disc
error messages in the same file are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/Game/main.cpp b/src/Game/main.cpp
index 5814286..3f603a3 100644
--- a/src/Game/main.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/main.cpp
@@ -567,6 +567,12 @@ static void Initialize()
 #endif // DVD/reset registration remains outside this selected loading gate
 #if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP) || defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_LOADING_MESSAGE) \
     || (defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_INITIAL_LOADING_MESSAGE))
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port change, always on: no "Loading" bitmap between the port's graphics
+    // preparation and the boot scene. The output stays black until the boot
+    // scene's first swap turns it on (glxSwap).
+    if (false)
+#endif
     DisplayLoadingMessageFast();
 #endif
 #if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP) || defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_SEQUENCE)
